    {"id":"concept_field_code_protocol","label":"Logistics 4x4 field communication code protocol (D/H/X profiles)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/mnt/sda2/website/id/codes.html","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A compact letter+two-digit code protocol for use when data connectivity is unavailable, designed for truck drivers, hikers, and emergency services operating cross-border or in remote terrain. Three user profiles (Driver, Hiker, Emergency Services) share a common alert (A) and system (Z) vocabulary so cross-agency communication remains possible even in severely degraded conditions. Sharing the reference is explicitly encouraged because interoperability depends on all parties knowing the codes."},
