    {"id":"concept_ripa_2000_call_recording","label":"UK RIPA 2000 / Telecommunications (Lawful Business Practice) call-recording notification law","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/mnt/sda2/website/id/classroom.html","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Under RIPA 2000 and the Telecommunications (Lawful Business Practice) Regulations, a party recording a call may do so without the other party's consent for their own lawful use, but for the recording to be admissible in court all parties must be notified before recording begins. The Companion app enforces this by showing a persistent RECORDING banner to all connected participants whenever recording is active."}
